# EKS access patterns
AWS-0039
AWS-0040
AWS-0041

 
| Finding                                 | Decision                                | Why                                                                                                                                                                          |
| --------------------------------------- | --------------------------------------- | ---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------- |
| **AWS-0039 — Secrets encryption**       | No explicit `encryption_config`         | EKS Kubernetes 1.31 provides default envelope encryption. A customer-managed key is a separate control decision, adds unnecessary cost and not a critical requirement |
| **AWS-0040 — Public endpoint**          | Retain public access                    | Both dynamic-IP laptop and GitHub-hosted runners need to reach the EKS API.                                                                                              |
| **AWS-0041 — Unrestricted public CIDR** | Retain `0.0.0.0/0`                      | A narrow static allowlist does not currently accommodate both access paths reliably. Authentication and authorization are still required.                                    |
